# Migration wizard audit — verification gates

## 0. Concurrent-edit status of `worker/migrate-real.ts`

**It is actively being edited, but it is NOT structurally damaged.**

- Line count grew under me during the audit: 5743 → 5817 → 5845 → 5910; `mtime` advanced three times (last at 16:02:19Z).
- `ts.createSourceFile(...).parseDiagnostics` = **0 errors** at every snapshot; 183 top-level statements; braces/backticks balanced.
- No conflict markers (`<<<<<<<`), no `TODO`/`FIXME`/`XXX` stubs, no truncated functions, no unbalanced blocks.
- **False alarm I want to flag explicitly:** I initially thought the PostgreSQL import block + section `8b` were duplicated. They are not — two of my reads straddled two different file versions ~57 lines apart. Re-read as one snapshot, the block appears exactly once.

**Caveat on line numbers below:** they are from my last consistent read. The file has moved since. Each finding includes a distinctive snippet so it can be located regardless.

---

## FINDINGS

### F1 — HIGH: the SIMULATION runs in production and writes `DONE` / "Migration completed"

**`/opt/nxeon/worker/migrate.ts:20`** and **`/opt/nxeon/worker/migrate.ts:531-543`**

```ts
const REAL_MIGRATION = process.env.ENABLE_REAL_MIGRATION === "1" && !SANDBOX;
...
// ---- Progress-reporting SIMULATION of the lift-and-shift (default) --------
// Mirrors the real engine's flow ... with SYNTHETIC success.
await db.migration.update({
  where: { id: migration.id },
  data: { status: "DONE", progress: 100, step: "Completed", finishedAt: new Date() },
});
await notify(migration.userId, `Migration to ${targetName} completed`, ...)
```

The `else` branch is not sandbox-gated. If `ENABLE_REAL_MIGRATION` is unset/typo'd/lost on a redeploy in **production**, every migration walks a fake progress bar with `simResults.push({... status: "running", detail: "installed" })`, ends `DONE`, and MigrationWizard renders **"Migration complete 🎉"**. Nothing on either server was touched and no SSH connection was ever opened.

- **Customer sees:** "Migration to srv-x completed. 6 item(s) migrated & running." Green card. Told to point DNS.
- **What is true:** zero bytes moved. Their old server is the only copy; pointing DNS kills the site.
- This is the exact defect the team already fixed twice this week elsewhere: `worker/game-config.ts:71-79` ("Simulation is a SANDBOX affordance and MUST NEVER run in production… it stamped an `_appliedAt` marker and notified them") and `worker/ssl.ts:35-37` ("outside SANDBOX without the flag it FAILS LOUDLY"). Migration never got the same treatment.
- `.env:35` currently has `ENABLE_REAL_MIGRATION=1`, so this is latent today — one env regression from live.

**Smallest fix** — copy the `game-config.ts` guard verbatim, before the simulation block:
```ts
if (!REAL_MIGRATION && !SANDBOX) {
  throw new Error("Migration could not run: real migration is switched off on this server (ENABLE_REAL_MIGRATION is not set), so NOTHING was copied. Contact support.");
}
```

---

### F2 — HIGH: the post-cutover TLS pass has zero producers; the "we do HTTPS for you" promise is never kept

**`/opt/nxeon/worker/migrate.ts:258`** (docstring), **`:341-351`** (handler), **`/opt/nxeon/lib/actions-migrate.ts:427-433`** (the only enqueue)

```ts
// worker/migrate.ts:258 — "Enqueue it with:"
//   db.job.create({ data: { type: "MIGRATE", payload: { migrationId, phase: "tls" } } })

// lib/actions-migrate.ts:427 — the ONLY db.job.create for MIGRATE in the repo
await db.job.create({ data: { type: "MIGRATE", serverId: server.id, payload: { migrationId: migration.id } } });
```

`grep -rn 'phase: *"tls"'` across the whole repo returns **one hit: the comment**. `pointMigrationDns` (`lib/actions-migrate.ts:804-847`) — the exact moment DNS moves — writes an audit log and returns success, enqueuing nothing. Migrations also never create `Website`/`SslCertificate` rows, so `worker/ssl.ts`'s `sslSweep` cannot pick these hostnames up either.

Meanwhile the engine tells the customer, twice, in the run log and in every TLS pending item:

- `migrate-real.ts:5830` — `"2. Leave HTTPS to us. Nxeon issues or extends the certificate automatically within about 30 minutes of each DNS change — there is no certbot command for you to run."`
- `migrate-real.ts:3579` — `"…move its DNS to X now — Nxeon issues the certificate automatically within about 30 minutes of the change, and nothing else is needed."`

- **Customer sees:** an explicit instruction to do nothing, and a 30-minute SLA.
- **What is true:** no job exists, no scheduler fires, no certbot ever runs. First HTTPS visit after cutover is a full-page browser warning — the identical 2026-07-25 outcome `runPostCutoverTls` was written to prevent. Its own docstring says `issueMigrationCertificates` "had ZERO callers"; the fix added a consumer but never a producer.

**Smallest fix** — in `pointMigrationDns`, after `if (!res.ok) return …`:
```ts
await db.job.create({
  data: { type: "MIGRATE", serverId: m.serverId, payload: { migrationId, phase: "tls" }, runAt: new Date(Date.now() + 120_000) },
}).catch(() => {});
```
(Or drop the promise wording to match reality.)

