### F9 — MEDIUM: a totally failed source inventory can still score `COMPLETED` — and asserts a fact about the source it never measured

**`/opt/nxeon/worker/migrate-real.ts`** — the `if (!inv.probed)` branch (inventory section, ~`:3760`), `judgeMigrationOutcome` at **`:2484-2488`**, final summary at **`:5788`**

```ts
// inventory failure emits a LOG LINE only — no push(), so no `failed` step exists
if (!inv.probed) {
  await report(11, "Inspecting the old server…", "  Could not complete the inventory — continuing with what the original scan found.");
}

// judgeMigrationOutcome — the "we couldn't read the source" reason requires probeNames to be non-empty
if (!input.sourceDomains.length && input.probeNames.length) { outcomeReasons.push("the old server's live configuration could not be read…"); }

// :5788 — the COMPLETED headline when both sets are empty
: "everything selected was migrated and verified; the old server did not serve any websites, so there was nothing to publish",
```

For a files-only migration whose source inventory died (SSH hiccup, `sudo -n` denied, sweep timeout): `sourceDomains = []`, `servedSites = []`, `probeNames = []`, no `failed` steps → **outcome `COMPLETED`**. `test/migration-gate.test.ts:597` ("nothing to migrate is not an issue") deliberately locks in the empty-empty case, but the engine cannot distinguish "the source had no websites" from "we could not look".

- **Customer sees:** green "Migration complete 🎉" plus *"the old server did not serve any websites, so there was nothing to publish"*.
- **What is true:** we never read the old server's config. It may serve six domains, none of which exist here.

**Smallest fix:** thread the fact through the pure scorer —
```ts
// MigrationScoreInput
inventoryRead?: boolean;
// judgeMigrationOutcome
if (input.inventoryRead === false) outcomeReasons.push("the old server's live configuration could not be read at all, so we cannot say which sites it served — check by hand before moving DNS");
// call site :5666
inventoryRead: inv.probed,
```

