### F10 — LOW: file copies verify rsync's exit code only, never counts or bytes

**`/opt/nxeon/worker/migrate-real.ts:4256-4266`** (paths) and **`:4283-4292`** (volumes)

```ts
const r = await execRemote(conn, rsyncPull(p, destParent), TRANSFER_TIMEOUT_MS).catch(...);
if (r.code === 0) copied++;
...
if (copied) push({ step: `Copy ${copied} folder(s) to their original paths`, status: "copied", detail: "files placed at the same paths on the new server" });
```

Defensible — rsync returns 23/24 on partial transfers, so exit 0 is meaningful, and the step is honestly labelled `"copied"` rather than `"running"`. Flagging only because the brief asked. If you want the gate: `find <path> -type f | wc -l` and `du -sb <path>` on both ends, or a `rsync -n -ai --stats` second pass that must report zero remaining transfers.

